<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/11/nvalt-mermaid-header-rb.7540.jpg" width="800" height="226" style="margin:0 auto;clear:both;" class="header" /></p>
<p>Another update to nvALT. This is probably going to keep happening. Mermaid, MathJax, and updated documentation are included this time.</p>

<p>The <a href="https://brettterpstra.com/projects/nvalt/">nvALT project page</a> is the documentation now. Installation, search, tagging, the editor shortcuts, themes, and the Apex syntax the preview actually renders are all on one page.</p>

<p>The preview also typesets math and draws Mermaid diagrams.</p>

<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/11/nvalt-mermaid-800.jpg"></p>

<h3 id="math">Math</h3>

<p>Apex already understood the delimiters. The preview now runs MathJax on them.</p>

<p>Inline math sits in the sentence:</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code>The area of a circle is $A=\pi r^2$.</code></pre></div></div>

<p>A display equation gets its own lines:</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code>$$
E = mc^2
$$</code></pre></div></div>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">\(...\)</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">\[...\]</code> work the same way. <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">$40</code> stays a price, because Apex treats a dollar sign followed by a digit as currency.</p>

<h3 id="diagrams">Diagrams</h3>

<p>A fenced block tagged <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">mermaid</code> becomes a diagram:</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code>```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A[Note] --&gt; B[Preview]
  B --&gt; C[MathJax]
  B --&gt; D[Mermaid]
```</code></pre></div></div>

<p>That is the one diagram type the preview draws. A Graphviz block stays a code block.</p>

<h3 id="bundled-and-only-when-the-note-needs-them">Bundled, and only when the note needs them</h3>

<p>MathJax 4 and Mermaid 12 ship inside the app. The preview does not call out to a CDN, so a note still renders on a plane.</p>

<p>A note with no math and no Mermaid fence does not load either library. Open a note that has one of them and that library comes along. Open a note that has both and you get both.</p>

<p>Each time the preview updates, it reloads the whole page. MathJax and Mermaid start over with that reload. The scroll position is the thing that carries across.</p>

<p>The HTML source view, and Save Preview HTML, stay as the Apex markup. The libraries are there for the live preview.</p>

